{
  "group": "capability-claims",
  "gate": null,
  "why": "Corrects live posts that promise things a generated site cannot do. Grounded in lib/agent.ts SYSTEM, which now (a) forbids building a contact/booking/newsletter/login/cart control that appears functional — 'a form that silently discards a real enquiry is worse than no form' — and directs the model to a mailto:, tel: or link-out instead; (b) states 'this is a single-page app', so a prompt asking for four pages does not get four pages; (c) forbids inventing testimonials, staff names, hours, prices or addresses for a real business. Add app/api/site/[slug]/[[...path]]/route.ts, whose CSP is default-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data'; connect-src 'none' — which rules out uploaded photography, remote galleries and map embeds. These are the highest-severity errors of the three groups: a reader acts on them by sending real patients at a form that throws their appointment away.",
  "detect": [
    "collects the request and sends it to you",
    "working (?:request |contact |booking |inquiry )?form",
    "form (?:UI )?with working input state",
    "submissions? (?:actually )?land",
    "multi-?page (?:site|app)",
    "(?:swap|replace|add) (?:them |the placeholders? )?(?:for|with) your own (?:real )?(?:photos|photography|images)",
    "map-style block",
    "photo gallery"
  ],
  "edits": [
    {
      "slug": "website-builder-for-dentists",
      "find": "A simple form where a patient enters their name, contact info, preferred day/time, and reason for the visit. Kodely can build you a genuinely good-looking, professional appointment-request page and contact form. To be clear about what that means today: it collects the request and sends it to you — it does not yet sync automatically to a calendar or scheduling system. Most small practices are fine with this as a starting point: the request comes in, your front desk confirms by phone or email, same as an inquiry from any other channel.",
      "replace": "One obvious, impossible-to-miss way to get in touch. Be precise about what that is, because it is the one thing on this page you must not get wrong: a Kodely site is front-end only, with no server and no mail sending behind it, so a form on it would silently discard every appointment request. The builder will not build one for that reason. What it will build is a large tap-to-call <code>tel:</code> button, an email link, and a prominent \"Book online\" button pointing at whatever scheduling system you already use. Those work the moment the site is live.",
      "note": "The old text said the form 'collects the request and sends it to you'. There is no backend and no mail path for generated sites; lib/agent.ts SYSTEM explicitly forbids building the control at all."
    },
    {
      "slug": "website-builder-for-dentists",
      "find": "Kodely can build a professional, well-designed appointment-request page and contact form. It collects the patient's request — it doesn't yet connect to a real calendar or scheduling backend automatically, so your team confirms the appointment manually, the same way you'd handle a phone or email inquiry.",
      "replace": "No, and it deliberately won't fake one. There is no backend behind a generated site, so a booking form would throw every request away — the builder is instructed not to produce a control that only pretends to work. Instead it gives you the parts that do work with no server: a tap-to-call number, an email link, and a button pointing at the booking system you already use.",
      "note": "FAQ answer. Same grounding."
    },
